From: Volodymyr Pavlenko <pavlenko.vv@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 21:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ath_client: ignore VLAN lifecycle events

VLAN netdevices emit their own register and unregister notifications. The
ATH client currently replaces the VLAN device with its WLAN real device
before dispatching the unchanged notification. As a result, registering a
VLAN tries to allocate the WLAN parent's VP again, while unregistering the
VLAN can free the still-active parent's VP.

VLAN lifecycle is handled by the PPE VLAN manager. Ignore VLAN register and
unregister notifications in the ATH client before resolving the real
device.

Signed-off-by: Volodymyr Pavlenko <pavlenko.vv@pm.me>
---
 clients/ath_client/nss_ppe_ath_client.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clients/ath_client/nss_ppe_ath_client.c b/clients/ath_client/nss_ppe_ath_client.c
--- a/clients/ath_client/nss_ppe_ath_client.c
+++ b/clients/ath_client/nss_ppe_ath_client.c
@@ -130,6 +130,15 @@ static int nss_ppe_ath_client_netdevice_event(struct notifier_block *unused,
 	struct netdev_notifier_info *info = (struct netdev_notifier_info *)ptr;
 	struct net_device *dev = netdev_notifier_info_to_dev(info);
 
+	/*
+	 * VLAN interfaces are handled by the PPE VLAN manager. Do not turn a
+	 * VLAN lifecycle event into a lifecycle event for its WLAN real device.
+	 */
+	if (is_vlan_dev(dev) &&
+		(event == NETDEV_REGISTER || event == NETDEV_UNREGISTER)) {
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+	}
+
 	dev = is_vlan_dev(dev) ? vlan_dev_real_dev(dev) : dev;
 	if (!dev->ieee80211_ptr) {
 		nss_ppe_ath_client_info("Dev: %s not a WLAN dev\n", dev->name);
-- 
